The GNOME Series contains the GNOME desktop environment and related libraries.

Installation sudo apt install task-gnome-desktop gnome-backgrounds vanilla-gnome-desktop gnome-boxes gnome-shell-extensions -y
After install run sudo apt remove desktop-base -y
then sudo apt autoremove -y
then sudo apt purge desktop-base -y
then sudo apt autoremove -y

When opening the terminal
Open Preferences then change Palette Ubuntu To GNOME (Default) or change anything you want (If you want it) or you can keep the palette Ubuntu (If you want it)

If update are changing accent color to orange you can change the color back to blue

pin gnome web evolution and text editor to dash like standard gnome

If there is memtest86+ but you are running UEFI you can remove with sudo apt purge memtest86+ -y then sudo update-grub then sudo apt autoremove -y (UNLESS YOU ARE RUNNING ON LEGACY BIOS)

For i686
Make sure you have enough storage and ram

Installation sudo apt install gnome-session gnome gdm gnome-terminal gnome-software -y
Then run sudo apt remove desktop-base -y
Then run sudo apt purge desktop-base -y
Then sudo apt autoremove -y
Then Add GNOME Software to Favorites
